[
  {
    "_comment": "CAPABILITY suite for the local-file connector (all data formats + source selection modes), via `--type connectors/localfile.json`. Functions in functions/caps_localfile.py. FLOW: `caps_input` (dev datagen) publishes cap_rows; the `localfile_out` subscribers write it to the `fs` domain root in every format (CSV/JSON/AVRO/PARQUET + a CSV with custom format_cfg). The `localfile_in` publishers exercise wildcard/last-modified/multi/none over the seeded world parquet in `fs_world_xs`. TWO-PHASE: after the first `run` commits (files written), trigger the `localfile_rt` round-trip readers (they read each written file back with the matching format; not auto-triggered because the files must exist first). `fs` (writers+round-trip) and `fs_world_xs` (seed readers) are distinct domains; dev backs the datagen input. SRC METADATA: localfile_meta_keep and localfile_meta_drop (localfile_in) read the same staged country parquet with and without the `tabsdata.src_metadata.drop` src_cfg key, and one transformer each in collection localfile_meta (group ops) asserts that side: localfile_meta_keep_check that the `@td.file.path` metadata column is there plus exactly the expected data columns, localfile_meta_drop_check that no `@td.` column is left and the data columns are unchanged (functions/_srcmeta.py — which also explains why ONE transformer over both tables cannot work: an input reference puts the function in the producing plan, so it would run in each publisher's plan with the other's table missing)."
  },
